#!/usr/bin/env bash
# gh — intentional shim that shadows any real GitHub CLI on PATH.
#
# This machine never uses `gh`. See:
#   ~/.dotfiles/CLAUDE.md  (house rules)
#
# Exists as a defense-in-depth backup to the Bash(gh) / Bash(gh *)
# entries in ~/.dotfiles/claude/settings.json — if an LLM somehow
# bypasses the permission deny, this shim still stops the call and
# tells the agent what to do instead.

cat <<'EOF' >&2
gh is intentionally disabled on this machine.

For any GitHub operation (PRs, issues, comments, releases, workflows,
repo metadata), use the MCPLocker GitHub MCP tools instead:

    mcp__claude_ai_MCPLocker__github__*

For plain local git work (status / log / diff / commit / push /
fetch / etc.), use the real `git` binary — that's fine. Only `gh`
is blocked.

If you are an LLM that just tried to run gh: stop, switch to the MCP
tools, and continue. Don't try to invoke the real gh binary by
absolute path — this rule is not a bug.
EOF

exit 127
